& [ClosedSupport] is exact
  + strict M2A topology forms distinguish structural validity from admission
  + supplied fixed-query and stream records assemble into an incomplete topology projection seed
  + two independently reassembled supplied metadata bundles reconcile through exact ordered comparison
  + exact caller-supplied chunks derive SHA-256 under checked byte and chunk budgets
  + supplied-byte derivation structurally binds to a newly reconciled stable regular-file pair through exact entry-reference and length gates
  + all successful content observations and bindings are output-only and preserve their complete lower-level evidence
  + current global debug and overflow-checked release evidence is 319 passed with one governed physical ignore

& [SupportDelta] closes content but not topology placement
  + [closed] exact digest derivation from supplied bytes and structural equality with supplied stable EOF values
  + [closed] stable regular-file kind and entry-reference correlation inside an unforgeable in-process binding
  + [still_open] relative-path placement and exact last-component correspondence
  + [still_open] Git executable-mode observation and reconciliation
  + [still_open] traversal-owned ordinal assignment and canonical inventory ordering
  + [still_open] physical byte acquisition, common owned-handle provenance, and actual pre-content-post order
  + [still_open] stream-enumeration completeness and physical query completion
  + [still_open] directory and whole-root repetition, Git control reconciliation, receipt production, and admission integration

& [ExistingFormMeaning] permits a bounded next composition
  + M2A TopologyEntryObservation is explicitly a caller-supplied structurally coherent form
  + M2A states that valid form does not mean admitted entry
  + relative_path, mode_class, and observation_ordinal are already caller-owned structural fields at this layer
  + the supplied assembly seed deliberately omitted those fields until a later separately validated composition
  + the supplied content binding now supplies the previously missing derived digest without accepting an asserted digest
  = therefore: a labeled supplied projection may construct and preserve a complete M2A form without claiming scanner provenance

& [CandidateComparison] is dependency ordered
  + [candidate_A] is implement the physical Windows metadata and content producer
    - rejected because owned-handle provenance, initialized buffers, query completion, actual temporal order, and physical fixtures remain a larger unsafe-adjacent authority boundary
  + [candidate_B] is construct a bare TopologyEntryObservation from arbitrary caller values
    - rejected because it could bypass the output-only content binding and erase the distinction between declared and derived facts
  + [candidate_C] is pure supplied regular-file topology projection from the output-only content binding plus a strict placement plan
    + consumes the successful binding rather than accepting an asserted digest or publicly constructible stable pair
    + validates exact entry-reference equality and exact final-component equality against the previously admitted component
    + admits only regular mode classes and a nonzero caller-declared ordinal
    + constructs and validates the complete M2A structural form
    + preserves the complete placement plan, content binding, and projected form in an output-only wrapper
    + keeps path, Git mode, ordinal, stream completeness, physical origin, and traversal explicitly caller-supplied or unresolved
  + [candidate_D] is pure directory or whole-root inventory reconciliation
    - deferred because no complete supplied entry-projection carrier yet preserves path, ordinal, and lower-level evidence together
  + [candidate_E] is exact Git executable-mode reconciliation
    - deferred because it requires a separately defined Git inventory evidence vocabulary and producer boundary
  + [candidate_F] is receipt or admission composition
    - rejected because traversal, repeated inventory, Git reconciliation, physical provenance, and freshness are not closed

& [SelectedBoundary] is pure supplied regular-file topology projection
  + [working_profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-regular-file-topology-projection/0.1
  + [plan] contains exact profile, nonzero projection identity, nonzero entry-reference identity, canonical descendant relative path, regular mode class, and nonzero observation ordinal
  + [binding_input] is WindowsSuppliedContentStableBinding by value
  + [entry_reference_gate] requires exact plan and binding equality
  + [component_gate] requires the final relative-path component to equal the stable pair policy component exactly
  + [projection] derives kind, attributes, identity, link count, streams, and length from the stable pair projection seed; derives content digest only from the supplied-content observation; and copies path, mode, and ordinal only from the plan
  + [validation] applies the current ValidateTopologyForm implementation to the completed M2A form
  + [output] is private-field, Serialize-only, non-Deserialize, non-default, and non-publicly-constructible; it preserves the exact plan, complete binding, and complete M2A projection
  + [fault] is one closed bounded value with an exact nested topology-form fault only when M2A validation rejects
  + [Cargo_delta] is zero
  - never: accept an asserted content digest, a bare stable pair, or a bare projection seed as sufficient input
  - never: expose From or Into conversion that loses the wrapper and its provenance grade
  - never: claim the path was traversed, the mode came from Git, the ordinal was assigned by a scanner, or the streams are physically complete
  - never: claim bytes, metadata, path, mode, or ordinal refer to one physical object or epoch
  - never: issue a receipt or admission result

& [SemanticGrade] remains supplied structural projection
  + [derived] kind, attributes, identity, link count, stream facts, length, and SHA-256 are transformations of previously accepted supplied values
  + [declared] relative path, Git mode class, observation ordinal, projection identity, and entry-reference identity are caller syntax
  + [correlated] means exact equality and structural relation under this profile only
  + [projected] means a valid M2A form nested beside all source evidence in one output-only wrapper
  + [physical] remains absent
  + [admitted] remains absent

& [FailureBoundary] is fail closed
  + oversized or malformed JSON, unknown fields, unknown profile, zero identities, empty or malformed path, disallowed mode, or zero ordinal reject
  + entry-reference mismatch rejects before projection
  + final-component mismatch rejects before projection
  + any M2A structural fault is preserved as a nested topology-form fault
  + no successful wrapper or partially projected entry accompanies a fault

